---
import SideCard from './SideCard.astro';

// The home page intro, shown as a card in the right sidebar (`card: home`).
// Neutral structure; pink and green only where they mean something (see /design).
// One tile per example on the home page, linking to its section. The pink dot marks a problem.
const examples = [
	['TLA+', 'double connect', '#connect-on-first-use'],
	['Quint', 'late reply', '#search-as-you-type'],
	['Dafny', 'missed id', '#binary-search-over-sorted-ids'],
	['Lean', 'negative price', '#a-percentage-discount'],
];
---

<SideCard>
	<p class="eyebrow">Formal methods for TypeScript</p>
	<p class="story"><strong>A small part of a TS codebase may become unmanageable.</strong> We usually are comfortable with 95% of a project's code, but one or two small pieces are getting out of hand: scary to change, impossible to describe, and painful to test.</p>
	<p class="story"><strong>Formal methods first of all bring thinking/comprehension tools.</strong> They make some systems easier to understand and the ability to change them without even having to fully understand. Correctness is a result.</p>
	<p class="story"><strong>The TS ecosystem falls short, but the industry has a lot to offer.</strong> TLA+, Quint, Dafny, Lean and more. Here we will try to bridge the gap and show how to use a wide selection of tools in a TypeScript project.</p>
	<p class="story"><strong>Formal methods are getting easier for developers to adopt.</strong> They used to need special knowledge. Now AI assistants and tools native to programming languages make them friendly to software engineers.</p>
	<div class="examples">
		<p class="examples-title">Practical examples</p>
		<ul>
			{
				examples.map(([tool, problem, href]) => (
					<li>
						<a href={href}>
							<b>{tool}</b>
							<span>{problem}</span>
						</a>
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ul>
	</div>
</SideCard>

<style>
	/* Links to the examples below. */
	.examples {
		margin-top: 1.25rem;
		padding-top: 1rem;
		border-top: 1px dashed var(--sc-border);
	}
	.examples-title {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.examples ul {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0.65rem 0 0;
		padding: 0;
	}
	.examples a {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.1rem;
		padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--sc-border);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		background: var(--sc-bg);
		color: var(--sc-text);
		text-decoration: none;
		line-height: 1.25;
		transition: border-color 0.15s;
	}
	.examples a:hover,
	.examples a:focus-visible {
		border-color: var(--sc-text);
	}
	.examples b {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
	}
	.examples a span {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.35rem;
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		white-space: nowrap;
		color: var(--sc-muted);
	}
	.examples a span::before {
		content: '';
		width: 0.4rem;
		height: 0.4rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: var(--sc-pink);
		flex: none;
	}

	@media (max-width: 71.99rem) {
		.examples ul {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
		}
	}
</style>
